   <taskbody>  <context>
    <p>X-Author for Excel Designer has been enhanced with the following features grouped under a Centralized Admin. This new centralized admin enables you to configure and administer various settings related to the Designer.</p><ul>
         <li>
            <xref href="#usingcentralizedadmingeneralinfo">General Info</xref>
         </li>
         <li>
            <xref href="#usingcentralizedadminsettings">Settings</xref>
         </li>
         <li>
            <xref href="#usingcentralizedadminproductlogs">Product Logs</xref>
         </li>
         <li>
            <xref href="#usingcentralizedadmincrmmessages">CRM Messages</xref>
         </li>
         <li>
            <xref href="#usingcentralizedadminconnections">Connections</xref>
         </li>
         <li>
            <xref href="#usingcentralizedadminapp">App</xref>
         </li>
      </ul><p>This section displays general information on X-Author for Excel such as User info, version, and Available X-Author Add-ins.</p><fig>
         <title>190354365</title>
         <image href="../attachments/98687460/190354365.png" width="1138" height="641" placement="break">
            <alt>placeholder</alt>
         </image>
      </fig><p>This section enables you to set up <xref href="../general_settings_98687609/general_settings.dita">general settings</xref> such as changing CRM, language, and Proxy Settings.</p><fig>
         <title>190354367</title>
         <image href="../attachments/98687460/190354367.png" width="1138" height="641" placement="break">
            <alt>placeholder</alt>
         </image>
      </fig><p>This section <xref href="../viewing_product_logs_98687623/viewing_product_logs.dita">displays all the logs</xref> in the event of an error.</p><fig>
         <title>190354372</title>
         <image href="../attachments/98687460/190354372.png" width="1138" height="641" placement="break">
            <alt>placeholder</alt>
         </image>
      </fig><p>This section <xref href="../viewing_crm_specific_logs_98687632/viewing_crm_specific_logs.dita">displays all the CRM specific logs</xref> in the event of an error.</p><fig>
         <title>190354373</title>
         <image href="../attachments/98687460/190354373.png" width="1138" height="641" placement="break">
            <alt>placeholder</alt>
         </image>
      </fig><p>This section displays all the available connections. You can change the connection name or delete a particular connection.</p><fig>
         <title>98687467</title>
         <image href="../attachments/98687460/98687467.png" width="1138" height="641" placement="break">
            <alt>placeholder</alt>
         </image>
      </fig><p>This section displays the following information:</p><ul>
         <li>
            <b>App Details</b> - Provides details of the App such as App Name, Unique Id of the App, and whether the App is active or not.

<fig>
               <title>190354370</title>
               <image href="../attachments/98687460/190354370.png" placement="break" width="1138" height="641">
                  <alt>placeholder</alt>
               </image>
            </fig>

This section enables you to change the App Name and also activate or deactivate an app. The Unique Id field is a read-only field.</li>
         <li>
            <b>App Settings</b> - The following options are used to affect the runtime user experience, use protected worksheets, and secure Excel file saving and printing. For details, see <xref href="../application_settings_98667714/application_settings.dita">Application Settings</xref>.

<fig>
               <title>190354370</title>
               <image href="../attachments/98687460/190354370.png" placement="break" width="1138" height="641">
                  <alt>placeholder</alt>
               </image>
            </fig>
         </li>
         <li>
            <b>App Assignment</b> - After you have created an app and activated it, you need to <xref href="../activating_and_assigning_apps_98667701/activating_and_assigning_apps.dita">assign the app to runtime users</xref>.

<fig>
               <title>190354368</title>
               <image href="../attachments/98687460/190354368.png" placement="break" width="1138" height="641">
                  <alt>placeholder</alt>
               </image>
            </fig>
         </li>
      </ul>
